    "terminalReason": "completed",
    "text": "The search engine is built and working in the image. All 19 tests pass: my 14 in `BuscadorTest` plus the 5 starter tests for `todasLasCombinaciones`. I wrote each test before its code, saw it fail, then made it pass.\n\n**What it does** (classes in `2025-2C-Recuperatorio`, tests in `2025-2C-Recuperatorio-Tests`):\n- **Searches:** `Buscador` handles one-way, round-trip and multi-leg searches. One-way is a one-leg search and round-trip a two-leg search, so there is only one search logic. Each leg (`Tramo`) finds the flights that fly that route on that day of the week.\n- **Availability:** only flights with enough seats for the passengers are offered, according to the passenger counter.\n- **Legs in order:** `todasLasCombinaciones` combines the legs' flights. A combination is only offered if every flight leaves after the previous one arrives.\n- **What a trip shows:** a `Viaje` gives the origin, final destination, departure and arrival date-times, gross cost, net cost and the list of applied discounts with their amounts.\n- **Discounts:** `DescuentoPorFechaEspecial` and `DescuentoPorTramo` share a `Descuento` superclass. Each is applied per flight, always over that flight's gross, so several discounts can apply at once.\n\n**Assumptions to check:**\n- **Cost per passenger:** I read a flight's cost as the price of one ticket, so a trip's gross is the cost times the number of passengers. If you meant cost per flight regardless of passengers, it's a one-line change in `DefinicionDeVuelo>>costoPara:`.\n- **Percentages are plain numbers** (e.g. `10`), because Aconcagua has no percentage unit.\n- **Passenger counter:** the only thing the search engine asks it is `asientosDisponiblesPara: unCodigo el: unaFecha`. In the tests, the test case itself answers that message. There is no real REST client class, since no test could drive one.\n\nNothing has been saved. The `2025` package has unsaved changes and no file set, and I didn't save the image. Tell me if you want either done."
